#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:28
msgid "Using the hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:30
msgid ""
"Snapd uses the {ref}`hook <reference-development-supported-snap-hooks>` "
"mechanism in the kernel snap to run hook-specific executable binaries. The "
"first retrieves the encryption key and unlocks the disk while the second is "
"called on installation/re-installation to ensure the key is sealed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:32
msgid ""
"The first binary is executed from the initrd and is located inside the "
"_initrd_ $PATH, e.g. `usr/bin/fde-reveal-key`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:34
msgid ""
"This is used by snap-bootstrap initramfs-mounts to retrieve the key and "
"unlock the disk. It does not run with typical snapd confinement, using "
"systemd mechanisms instead to restrict the helper and ensure it is not "
"misused to change the ubuntu-data partition in uncontrolled ways."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:36
msgid ""
"The second binary is executed from the install/reinstall process to ensure "
"the key is sealed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:38
msgid ""
"It is run as a normal hook `meta/hooks/fde-setup` from the kernel snap with "
"corresponding `snapctl fde-setup-request` and `snapctl fde-setup-result` "
"commands that can be used from the hook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:40
msgid ""
"If `fde-reveal-key` and `meta/hooks/fde-setup` exist, they're used for all "
"FDE operations instead of the built-in TPM code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:42
