msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:43
msgid "Data handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:45
msgid ""
"The helper mechanism is stateless, with snapd providing whatever data is "
"necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:47
msgid ""
"When protecting a key, for instance, `fde-setup` returns a \"handle\" "
"consisting of any valid JSON, such as a string with base64-encoded binary "
"data, which could then be used as auxiliary data to help unseal/decrypt the "
"protected key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:49
msgid ""
"Apart from ensuring the data is valid JSON, or when the data is passed back "
"to `fde-reveal-key` (see below), snapd stores and handles this data "
"completely opaquely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:51
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-reveal-key\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:51
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-reveal-key\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:52
msgid "Data for fde-reveal-key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:54
msgid ""
"As mentioned earlier, the `fde-reveal-key` binary is run from _initrd_. It "
"gets data via _stdin_ and outputs the data to stdout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:56
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-reveal\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:56
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-reveal\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:57
msgid "op: reveal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:59
msgid ""
"In this operation the revealed key is written to _stdout_. The data passed "
"via _stdin_ is JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:61
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"op\": \"reveal\",                 // more may be added in the future\n"
"    \"sealed-key\": \"<base64-encoded-bytes>\",\n"
"    \"handle\": <handle-valid-json>,  // opaque handle (can be empty)\n"
"                                    // as returned previously by fde-setup\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:70
msgid ""
"It returns: `{\"key\": \"base64 encoded key\"}` to allow additional future "
"capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:72
#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:122
msgid ""
"Any exit code other than `0` is expected to return an error string to "
"_stderr_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:74
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-lock\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:74
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-lock\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:75
msgid "op: lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:77
msgid ""
"When the hook is called in this way, access to the keys should be locked "
"using a method appropriate for the underlying hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:79
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-setup\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:79
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde-setup\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:80
msgid "Data for fde-setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:82
msgid ""
"`fde-setup` is a normal snapd hook and uses {ref}`snapctl <how-to-guides-"
"manage-snaps-use-snapctl>` to communicate with snapd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:84
msgid ""
"The workflow for the hook is that it calls `snapctl fde-setup-request` and "
"reads the JSON from _stdout_. The JSON will contain an `op` field that tells "
"the hook what to do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:86
msgid ""
"The result is operation dependent and should be set via _stdin_ to `snapctl "
"fde-setup-result`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:88
msgid "<span id=\"heading--features\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:88
msgid "<span id=\"heading--features\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:89
msgid "op: features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:91
msgid ""
"If the `fde-setup` hook is run with `\"op\": \"features\"` (see above), the "
"hook should report, via JSON, a JSON-formatted array containing the features "
"it supports. Initially this will just be an empty list: `[]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:93
msgid "For example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:95
msgid ""
"$ snapctl fde-setup-request\n"
"{\"op\":\"features\"}\n"
"\n"
"$ echo '{\"features\": []}' | snapctl fde-setup-result\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:102
msgid "Currently, this is mostly to future proof hooks/snapd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:104
msgid "<span id=\"heading--initial-setup\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:104
msgid "<span id=\"heading--initial-setup\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:105
msgid "op: initial-setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:107
msgid ""
"If the `fde-setup` hook is run with `\"op\": \"initial-setup\"`, the hook "
"should call `snapctl fde-setup-request`, passing the following JSON to "
"_stdout_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:109
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"op\": \"initial-setup\",      // valid: \"initial-setup\",\"update\"\n"
"    \"key\": <base64-encoded-payload-that-should-be-encrypted/sealed>,\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:116
msgid "When the hook has completed the encryption and sealing, it will call:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/uc20-fde-hooks.md:118
msgid ""
"$ echo '{\"sealed-key\": \"<base64-sealed-or-encrypted-key>\", \"handle\": "
"<opaque-handle-valid-JSON> }' | snapctl fde-setup-result\n"
msgstr ""

